 funky: Express Yourself"],"pages":[[1,146]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"Funk: The Music, the People, and the Rhythm of the One","author":"Rickey Vincent","page":146,"text":"…legacy of the great Sam Cooke, Mayfield’s Chicago soul mentor). There were other smooth crooners that dabbled in social commentary, like the Stylistics with “People Make the World Go Round” in 1972, the Chi-Lites with “Give More Power to the People” in 1971, Bloodstone with “This World Is Funky,”…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Bloodstone Comparison","body":"Bloodstone's song \"Natural High\" is stylistically reminiscent of The Stylistics' song \"Betcha by Golly, Wow,\" particularly for its beautiful harmonies. \"Just listen and see if this does remind you of Betch by Golly Wild by the stylistics.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 46 - The Chaos and Music of the Ozark Music Festival of 1974","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 46 - The Chaos and Music of the Ozark Music Festival of 1974","url":"https://www.ftr70.com/"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":113663818728259,"type":"album","name":"The Stylistics","list_id":85048702844562,"list":"RYM Top — R&B","src":"musthear","rank":149,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"nAD-7wG5OZs","scaruffi":null},{"id":113663818728259,"type":"album","name":"The Stylistics","list_id":264682288693573,"list":"RYM Top — R&B — Philly Soul","src":"musthear","rank":2,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"nAD-7wG5OZs","scaruffi":null},{"id":113663818728259,"type":"album","name":"The Stylistics","list_id":126751190489920,"list":"RYM Top — R&B — Smooth Soul","src":"musthear","rank":17,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"nAD-7wG5OZs","scaruffi":null},{"id":113663818728259,"type":"album","name":"The Stylistics","list_id":202254272888124,"list":"RYM Top — R&B — Soul","src":"musthear","rank":92,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"nAD-7wG5OZs","scaruffi":null},{"id":243528879612419,"type":"song",